UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>This course provides science graduates and food industry employees with the opportunity to develop a suite of theoretical and practical skills while working in a real food processing environment at the Murdoch Food Centre which is part of the Food Innovation Precinct Western Australia (FIPWA).</p> <p>You’ll learn hands-on from experienced academic and food industry leaders to give yourself a competitive edge in the industry. Successful completion of the Graduate Diploma can provide an option of progressing onto a Master of Food Science.</p> <p><strong>3 reasons to study a Graduate Diploma in Food Science at Murdoch</strong></p> <ol><li>Study hands-on at Murdoch’s Food Centre that is part of the Food Innovation Precinct Western Australia (FIPWA).</li><li>Study at a university rated 5-star for student support at both undergraduate and postgraduate level by the Good Universities Guide 2026.*</li><li>Choose full-time, part-time to help you fit study into your working life and complete the course in as little as one year.</li></ol> <p><strong>What You’ll Learn:</strong></p> <ul><li>Food engineering and how to analyse and communicate how raw materials and processing affects final food product quality and nutrition.</li><li>Food safety and how to adapt food production processes to incorporate risk analysis and food safety planning.</li><li>Food product design solutions to address problems in, or improve, food products and systems (product development, quality improvement, shelf-life extension or engineering optimisation).</li><li>Key principles of human nutrition including food sources of nutrients and the effect of bioactive food components on health.</li></ul> <p><strong>Your career</strong></p> <p>The Graduate Diploma in Food Science will allow you to take your career in the food industry to the next level. You may be able to secure senior roles in Food Quality Assurance, Food Safety or New Product Development. Additional employment opportunities also exist in companies that service the food industry such as chemistry-based analytical or biological laboratories or food ingredient suppliers.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = NULL,
    offshore_tuition_fee = 43730,
    onshore_tuition_fee = 11009,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '',
    apply_form = 'https://www.murdoch.edu.au/course/Postgraduate/g1095',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '114433E';
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p><strong>Turn your compassion into a career with a </strong><strong>social care degree</strong> </p> <p>If you want to make a meaningful difference in people’s lives, our Bachelor of Applied Social Care prepares you to work across the growing care and community services sector. Our people-centred degree develops the knowledge, interpersonal skills and professional capabilities you’ll need to support individuals, families and communities in diverse care and human services environments. </p> <p>Throughout your applied social care degree, you’ll explore areas such as human rights, social justice, communication, ethical practice and relationship-based care. You’ll learn how to support people experiencing vulnerability, disadvantage or complex life challenges while building the reflective and practical skills needed in contemporary care environments. </p> <p>You can tailor your Bachelor of Applied Social Care to your interests and career goals by choosing a major in Human Rights, Child and Family Studies or Foundations of Business Management. </p> <p>Developed in consultation with industry and community partners, our social care course reflects the changing needs of Australia’s expanding care sector. You’ll build practical skills through real-world learning experiences and graduate prepared to contribute across community organisations, government services, social support services and not-for-profit settings. </p> <p>By the time you graduate, you’ll have the adaptability, empathy and professional knowledge needed for a rewarding career in social care and community support. </p> <p><strong>3 reasons to </strong><strong>study social care</strong><strong> at Murdoch University</strong> </p> <ul><li>Explore a degree in social care co-designed with industry and community partners to reflect the evolving needs of Australia’s growing care sector. </li><li>Study at the university ranked #1 in Western Australia for full-time employment, median salary and student support in Humanities and Social Sciences (<em>Good Universities Guide 2026</em>). </li><li>Learn at a university rated five stars for student support at both undergraduate and postgraduate level (<em>Good Universities Guide 2026</em>). </li></ul> <p><strong>What you’ll learn</strong> </p> <ul><li>Understand social care principles including ethical practice, human rights and social justice. </li><li>Develop communication and interpersonal skills to support individuals, families and communities. </li><li>Apply evidence-based approaches to respond to complex social care challenges. </li><li>Build reflective practice and professional self-awareness for contemporary care environments. </li><li>Analyse social care policies and practices across local, national and global contexts. </li><li>Design practical interventions that promote wellbeing, inclusion and community support. </li></ul> <p><strong>Your future </strong><strong>career in social care</strong> </p> <p>Our applied social care degree prepares you for a community care career across human services, disability support, youth and family services, mental health, advocacy and care coordination. You may also pursue further postgraduate study in areas such as public policy, development or social research. </p> <p><strong>Potential roles include:</strong></p> <ul><li>Community support worker </li><li>Disability support worker </li><li>Child and family support worker </li><li>Peer support worker </li><li>Care coordinator </li><li>Community services officer </li><li>Youth support worker </li><li>Social care advocate </li></ul> <p>For more details about our Bachelor of Applied Social Care, <a href="https://www.murdoch.edu.au/study/courses/admission-info/arts">download our information pack</a>. </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = NULL,
    offshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    enrolment_fee = NULL,
    materials_fee = NULL,
